  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercise_type\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"The concept of 'slow travel' has gained popularity in recent years, particularly among environmentally conscious tourists. Slow travel encourages visitors to stay in one place for a longer period, immersing themselves in the local culture and community. This approach not only reduces carbon emissions from frequent transportation but also allows travelers to develop a deeper understanding of the destination's history, customs, and way of life.\n\nIn contrast, mass tourism often prioritizes efficiency over authenticity, resulting in a superficial experience that fails to engage with the local environment. By adopting slow travel practices, tourists can contribute to the preservation of cultural heritage sites, support local economies, and foster meaningful connections with the people they meet.\n\nHowever, critics argue that slow travel can be elitist, catering only to those who have the financial means to afford extended stays in exotic locations. This criticism highlights the need for a more nuanced understanding of what slow travel entails and how it can be made accessible to a broader audience.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the article about slow travel?\",\n      \"options\": [\"It promotes mass tourism\", \"It encourages visitors to stay in one place for a longer period\", \"It reduces carbon emissions from frequent transportation\"],\n      \"answer\": \"It encourages visitors to stay in one place for a longer period\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"According to the article, what is a negative consequence of mass tourism?\",\n      \"options\": [\"It leads to job creation\", \"It results in a superficial experience that fails to engage with the local environment\", \"It promotes cultural exchange\"],\n      \"answer\": \"It results in a superficial experience that fails to engage with the local environment\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"The article mentions that slow travel can be elitist because it\",\n      \"options\": [\"Only caters to tourists from developed countries\", \"Caters only to those who have the financial means to afford extended stays in exotic locations\", \"Fosters meaningful connections with the local community\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Caters only to those who have the financial means to afford extended stays in exotic locations\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"The author's attitude towards slow travel is primarily\",\n      \"options\": [\"Critical and dismissive\", \"Supportive and encouraging\", \"Neutral and informative\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Supportive and encouraging\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"According to the article, what can slow travelers contribute to?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The preservation of cultural heritage sites\", \"The destruction of natural habitats\", \"The promotion of mass tourism\"],\n      \"answer\": \"The preservation of cultural heritage sites\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
